    "content": "Testing complete — all 19 checklist items executed and recorded.\n\n**Result: 14 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core product experience works well: dashboard creation and editing, venue/vendor filtering and live search, favorites, checklist browsing/saving, task completion, and localStorage persistence across reloads all behave correctly.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n1. **CS-8 — No budget validation.** Budget `0` and `-5000` both saved without error, overwriting the previously saved `$52,500` (dashboard rendered `$-5,000`).\n2. **CS-9 — No guest count validation.** `-30` and `88.6` both saved and displayed verbatim on the dashboard.\n3. **CS-11 — No wedding date validation.** The past date `2020-01-15` replaced the saved future date; the countdown element then disappeared entirely.\n4. **IX-12 — Detail views are non-functional.** \"View Details\" (venues) and \"View Profile\" (vendors) buttons produce no navigation, modal, or panel — they are inert buttons.\n5. **IX-19 — Cancel leaves a dirty draft.** Cancel correctly preserves the dashboard values, but the editor form is never reset, so reopening it shows the abandoned draft instead of the last saved values — a real data-loss risk, since a later Save would commit the stale draft.\n\nThe three constraint failures share one root cause: the wedding details form performs no validation at all before committing to state. Worth noting that IX-19 compounds this, as the un-reset form makes accidental bad saves more likely."
  }
}
